00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:56.600
I'll talk a little bit
more about that technology

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.460
later on as we learn.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:05.540
So coming back to last
lecture, what we talked

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.000
is a reciprocal space.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.810
That's a continuation and
proved the broad condition.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.100
And that's the, say, when you
do a transmission electron

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.940
microscope or you do an
X-ray, broad condition

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.330
is the one when you look
at diffraction patterns.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:28.490
And then we moved on
to discuss the energy

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.410
of the atomic
vibration in crystals.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:38.960
And so we introduce
the phonons, right?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.140
That's just the, say, we
solve the Newton second law.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.950
So first, it's a
continuum approach--

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.750
it's a classic approach.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:51.110
But trading the
atoms as discrete.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.950
And we got the dispersion
between the vibrational

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.550
frequency and wave vector.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:03.260
And the wave vector is similarly
as in the case of electron,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.165
are discretized.

00:03:05.165 --> 00:03:11.300
If I have [? any ?] atoms in the
chain, and I have 2 pi over n,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:15.350
the separation is 2 pi over
the length of the crystal.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.220
n times a is the length
of the crystal, right?

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.150
And we have acoustic branch.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.910
And if I have more than one
atom at the lattice point,

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.580
I have also
[? optical ?] branch.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:35.870
And the acoustic branch has a
longitudinal and transverse.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:41.060
Typically, longitudinal
has a higher frequency

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.120
and transfers lower frequency.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.790
And in the case of [? optical ?]
phonon, this sometimes

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.070
it can cross over.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:52.710
So it's hard to say which
one has a higher and lower.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.670
But I think if you deal
with the polar crystal,

00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:01.280
like sodium chloride, and
you have always a transverse

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.500
phonon lower and the
longitudinal phonon,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:06.470
[? optical ?] phonon
higher frequency.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:12.440
So what's important later on
is we'll simplify our models.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:16.220
And one way to
simplify is the Debye.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:18.440
So we [? try ?] this here.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.600
Although, the
[? zoom ?] boundary,

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:23.210
you can say we're careful
in drawing this almost

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:25.100
like a perpendicular.

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.550
But say, one
approximation we use

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:32.030
is [? approximated ?]
by a straight line.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.590
That's Debye model.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:39.360
And the other is what
original Einstein proposed

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.060
is just a constant frequency.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.840
That's an Einstein model.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.890
And you can see that
Einstein model is closer

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.890
for the [INAUDIBLE]
phonons, but Debye model

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:55.490
is closer for the
acoustical phonons.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.950
So that's where we were.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.220
And with that, if
you recall, what

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:03.890
we have talked to so
far, very fast, right,

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:09.050
we talked about energy levels,
first in isolated atoms

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.610
and molecules.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.520
And that's vibrational,
translational,

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.220
and electronic rotational.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:21.140
And then we extend
to crystals, and we

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:24.350
say the best treatment
[INAUDIBLE] is one dimension.

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:28.370
And then we say, OK, if you
look at the three dimension,

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:31.340
each direction has
different pure density

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:32.880
and different potential.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:36.080
So your curve may
look different, right?

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:42.320
And with that, I hope you get
appreciation for the energy

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.380
levels of electrons in solid.

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:47.210
With that, you
can understand why

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.030
there is the insulator, why
there are semiconductor,

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.280
why there are metals, right?

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:58.370
And also, you can now also
have some appreciation

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:02.070
for the large
vibration, the phonons,

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:05.550
which is essentially here
we do a classical treatment.

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.940
But what phonon is a quantized
form of this frequency.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:13.520
At each frequency for that mode,
you cannot have any energy.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:18.080
You can only have
discrete number of phonon.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.320
The energy is
quantized, all right?

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:25.790
So this gives us
some picture, what

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:31.230
are the quantum mechanical
allowable energy emitters?

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:36.830
And where we're going to
move is to add temperature

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.320
because this is a quantum
mechanical allowable.

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:43.250
Now, if I have an object
at a certain temperature,

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:48.680
what's the statistically
average, right?

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.940
And really, what's the
energy this object has?

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:56.720
So that's where we're moving.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.260
But before that, I want to
discuss a little bit more

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.790
of the content, right?

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:08.735
And if you recall, I said,
I emphasize degeneracy.

00:07:08.735 --> 00:07:16.490
A quantum state,
right, quantum state

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:21.080
is defined by, in
the case of waves,

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:26.090
is if I have wave
function in, let's

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:31.160
say I have my wave
function, and kx ky, kz.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:38.370
Each of this kx, ky, kz,
so here, for example,

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:43.190
in one direction I have discrete
number of k values, right?

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:48.500
Each combination of k value
gives me one specific wave,

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.720
of wave function, right?

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:56.040
One wave function is, if I
don't consider spin, right,

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.340
electron I have to say one wave
function because of the wave

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.740
function itself
doesn't include spin.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:07.000
So that's one quantum state, OK?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:11.950
And in the case
of discrete atoms,

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.690
we say quantum numbers, right?

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:18.140
If you recall, when we
do electronic states,

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:24.190
we have nlm, right?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.320
That's the quantum number.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.380
And we emphasize the
quant-- because it's

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:32.980
a different combination
of nlm could actually

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.190
have the same energy.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.679
That's where we
say this is how you

00:08:37.679 --> 00:08:41.460
start understand the periodic
table, right, the degeneracy.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:47.260
Now, if you look at solid, I'm
only drawing in one direction,

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:50.100
but we know that the
real crystal solid

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.150
is three directions.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:58.470
And now, if I count certain
frequency or certain energy--

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.450
if you think about either
frequency or energy

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.930
because [? H omega ?] gives
me some energy, right?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:07.650
And even in the same
direction, you can see here

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:14.080
I have three states,
three wave vectors

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:19.450
that can have same quantum
state, right, same energy.

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.570
Three wave vectors, three
quantum [? state can ?]

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.970
have same energy.

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:25.630
But if I look at the
other directions,

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.720
many, many other
directions, I would

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.320
have many other
possible states that

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:35.810
could have the same energy.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:38.560
So that's the
degeneracy, and that's

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:44.670
where I have to learn how
to do the counting, OK?

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:47.700
So this is a major
emphasis today.

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:53.580
It's the idea of counting.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:58.980
Today we're really doing
the density of states.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.450
And then when I
say states, I say

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:14.570
this is like density
of quantum states, OK?

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.770
And I also hope, at
the end, I have--

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:22.520
with that I'll get into
quantum statistics.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:39.870
So this is my plan
today, and let's start--

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:43.230
we have looked at a very
complicated band structure

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.790
for electrons, for phonons.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.490
This is like going
to the Google,

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.820
and you look at all those
different images, right?

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:53.580
But say, for the
analytical purpose,

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.500
we're going to look
at the simplest model,

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.300
like the Debye model.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.320
And for electrons,
we also say, if it's

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.170
at the minimum of
the conduction band

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:06.450
or the maximum of
the valence band,

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:09.690
we [? expend ?] that near
the minimum, maximum, right?

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.940
So we have parabolic bands.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:17.460
So we need this--

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:36.100
So if you'll recall for
electrons approximation,

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:42.030
and in the simplest
picture, this is my k.

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:46.330
And k, you can think
is a kx, ky, kz.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.710
And here is my
conduction band, and I

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:53.190
write this the minimum k
equals zero, minimum here.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.880
And you can put that at
a different point, OK?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:01.290
And this curvature
gives me effective mass.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:07.140
So if I say this is the energy
and expand this at the minimum,

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:13.380
then they are energy wave
[? actor ?] relation, right?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:17.740
And here is my E
C the bottom here.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:22.740
So energy [? wave ?] vector
relation is EC plus h bar k

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:26.610
square divide by 2 M star.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:31.170
So h bar k we say, under this--

00:12:31.170 --> 00:12:33.870
effective mass
concept, it's really

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:40.035
just like the 1/2 mv squared
because hk gives me momentum p.

00:12:40.035 --> 00:12:44.760
p divided by mass gives me--

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.800
gives the velocity, right?

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:52.240
So that's the parabolic
band approximation.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.620
And what we need
to keep in mind,

00:12:54.620 --> 00:13:00.570
the k is a vector
in 3D space, right?

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:05.580
So kx we said, if we
in the x direction,

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:12.765
is 2 pi n times Lx, right?

00:13:12.765 --> 00:13:17.250
And again, the end, if I
do all this parabolic band

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.530
approximation, my
[? zoom ?] boundary is here.

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:24.300
This is pi over ax, right?

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:29.670
[INAUDIBLE] x is how many
atoms times this appeared ax.

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:38.160
So let's say Lx equals n in
the x direction and periodicity

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:42.070
in the x direction, right?

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:44.770
That's how simple 1D model.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:49.360
Just to make a comment, by
passing, now some of you

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:53.650
probably do work in graphene.

00:13:53.650 --> 00:14:02.530
What's special with graphene
is that at the bottom here

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:08.950
the band here is not
quite a parabola.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.010
It's actually a
straight line, OK?

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:21.560
So graphene the dispersion,
this is the energy.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:22.660
This is wave vector.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:26.950
And in small region
near the Fermi level,

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.470
right, it's a zero gap.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:32.830
So the band gap
happened to be 0.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:38.720
And so at the Fermi level,
the dispersion is linear.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:41.290
And this linear
dispersion makes it

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:45.080
very similar to the
Debye model for phonon,

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.870
and also photon, right?

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:51.770
Photon is, if you think
about the model for photon,

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:56.210
is omega equals ck, right?

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.310
That's the speed of light.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:00.440
And for phonons,
omega equals vk.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.950
The v is the [? bi ?] velocity.

00:15:03.950 --> 00:15:07.830
Sometimes we associate with the
[? sun's ?] velocity, right?

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.420
So that makes the
electron similar to photon

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.270
and similar to phonons.

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:20.190
So that's what's special
with the graphene.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:26.210
So this is a kx, and of
course, I have a similar ky kz.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:31.190
And k squared is a
combination of kx

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:38.780
squared plus ky squared
plus kz squared, OK?

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:44.420
So this means, my
constant energy surface,

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:47.550
if I give k is a constant.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.690
Energy is a constant, right?
kx, ky, kz gives me a sphere.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:57.780
So is a spherical, say,
constant energy surface.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:16:00.840
Sometimes, if you draw
a real constant energy

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:03.180
surface in solid, it
look very complicated.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:07.940
Sometimes, it look like a
ellipsoid or even other shapes,

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.200
OK?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:11.220
But I'm doing the
simplest model.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:15.080
And so what you can
[? say ?] is there

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:18.080
are many combination
of kx, ky, kz

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.440
that could give me
the same energy E.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:25.140
And each combination
is one quantum state,

00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:27.230
including a factor of 2, If.

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:29.870
I think about spin, right?

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:36.440
So this is the dispersion, the
energy with vector relation

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:37.880
is dispersion.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:47.630
And for electrons
and for phonons,

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.390
we already said omega equals vk.

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:53.415
That's the [? bi ?]
approximation.

00:16:53.415 --> 00:16:59.730
And k, now, that's the k for the
electron-- for the phonon wave

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.230
vector.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.560
But again, based on
discussion we have,

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:08.540
those allowable values, right?

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:19.849
And for photon, omega equals
ck, like I just written down.

00:17:19.849 --> 00:17:26.464
But say, this k, for photon,
I don't have a upper limit.

00:17:29.085 --> 00:17:32.780
I haven't discussed--
so in free space,

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:37.420
this k could be
really large, OK?

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:43.780
So those are the dispersion
between frequency, wave vector,

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:45.220
or energy wave vector.

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:48.850
All those we call
dispersion relations, right?

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:52.700
Now, based on this, I'm going
to count how many states.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:58.750
So it turns out, for
